# Backend code formatting and style (.NET)

## EditorConfig rules

- **Indent**: 4 spaces for all C# files (`indent_size = 4`)
- **Encoding**: UTF-8-BOM (`charset = utf-8-bom`)
- **Line ending**: CRLF (`end_of_line = crlf`)
- **Trailing whitespace**: remove trailing spaces (`trim_trailing_whitespace = true`)
- **End of file**: always add a blank line at end of file (`insert_final_newline = true`)

## Using var

- **Use `var` everywhere** - use `var` for all local variables and parameters
- **Type must be obvious** - use explicit type only when type is not obvious from context

Example:
```csharp
// ✅ Correct
var request = command.Dto;
var recipientEmail = _configuration.GetValue<string>("EmailOptions:NotificationEmail");
var htmlBody = string.Empty;

// ❌ Incorrect
SubmitResumeDto request = command.Dto;
string recipientEmail = _configuration.GetValue<string>("EmailOptions:NotificationEmail");
string htmlBody = string.Empty;
```

## Naming

### Private fields
- **`_` prefix** - all private fields start with underscore and use camelCase
- **readonly fields** - private readonly fields also use `_` prefix

Example:
```csharp
private readonly IMediator _mediator;
private readonly ILogger<VacanciesController> _logger;
private readonly string[] _requiredPermissions;
```

### Public properties and methods
- **PascalCase** - all public properties and methods use PascalCase
- **Async methods** - all async methods must have `Async` suffix

Example:
```csharp
public string Name { get; set; }
public async Task<bool> HandleAsync(SubmitResumeCommand command, CancellationToken cancellationToken)
```

### Constants
- **PascalCase or ALL_UPPER** - constants may use PascalCase or ALL_UPPER with underscores

Example:
```csharp
private const string DefaultLanguage = "en";
private const int MAX_RETRY_COUNT = 3;
```

## Access modifiers

- **Always explicit** - always specify access modifiers (`private`, `public`, `protected`, `internal`)
- **Modifier order** - follow standard order: `public, private, protected, internal, static, readonly, async`

Example:
```csharp
public class VacanciesController : ControllerBase
{
    private readonly IMediator _mediator;
    protected override async Task<bool> HandleAsync(...)
}
```

## Braces

- **Always use braces** - even for single-line blocks
- **New line before opening brace** - opening brace on a new line

Example:
```csharp
// ✅ Correct
if (!ModelState.IsValid)
{
    foreach (var error in ModelState)
    {
        _logger.LogWarning("Error: {Key}", error.Key);
    }
}

// ❌ Incorrect
if (!ModelState.IsValid)
    _logger.LogWarning("Invalid");

if (!ModelState.IsValid) {
    _logger.LogWarning("Invalid");
}
```

## Control flow

- **New line before else** - `else` on a new line
- **New line before catch** - `catch` on a new line
- **New line before finally** - `finally` on a new line

Example:
```csharp
if (condition)
{
    DoSomething();
}
else
{
    DoSomethingElse();
}

try
{
    DoSomething();
}
catch (Exception ex)
{
    HandleError(ex);
}
finally
{
    Cleanup();
}
```

## Expression-bodied members

- **Methods** - use expression-bodied methods for simple one-line methods
- **Properties** - use expression-bodied properties for simple get-only properties
- **Constructors** - do not use expression-bodied constructors

Example:
```csharp
// ✅ Correct
public static string ToCamelCase(this string input)
    => Regex.Replace(input, "^[A-Z]", m => m.Value.ToLowerInvariant());

public string Name { get; set; } = string.Empty;

// ❌ Incorrect for constructors
public MyClass(string name) => _name = name;
```

## Modern C# features

### Pattern matching
- **Use pattern matching** - instead of `is` with cast, use pattern matching

Example:
```csharp
// ✅ Correct
var notSpecified = language switch
{
    "en" => "Not specified",
    "ru" => "Not specified",
    _ => "Not specified"
};

// ❌ Incorrect
string notSpecified;
if (language == "en")
    notSpecified = "Not specified";
else if (language == "ru")
    notSpecified = "Not specified";
else
    notSpecified = "Not specified";
```

### Null propagation
- **Use null propagation** - use `?.` and `??` for nullable types

Example:
```csharp
// ✅ Correct
var email = _configuration.GetValue<string>("EmailOptions:NotificationEmail")
             ?? _configuration.GetValue<string>("EmailOptions:FromUserAddress");
var permissions = headersContextAccessor.UserPermissions?
    .Any(claim => claim.Contains(permission)) ?? false;

// ❌ Incorrect
string email;
if (_configuration.GetValue<string>("EmailOptions:NotificationEmail") != null)
    email = _configuration.GetValue<string>("EmailOptions:NotificationEmail");
else
    email = _configuration.GetValue<string>("EmailOptions:FromUserAddress");
```

### Object and Collection initializers
- **Use initializers** - use object and collection initializers instead of multiple assignments

Example:
```csharp
// ✅ Correct
var command = new SubmitResumeCommand
{
    Dto = request ?? new SubmitResumeDto()
};

var parameters = new Dictionary<string, string>
{
    { "name", request.Name },
    { "email", request.Email }
};

// ❌ Incorrect
var command = new SubmitResumeCommand();
command.Dto = request ?? new SubmitResumeDto();
```

## Whitespace

- **After keywords** - space after keywords in control flow (`if`, `for`, `while`, `catch`)
- **Around operators** - spaces around binary operators (`+`, `-`, `==`, `!=`, `&&`, `||`)
- **After cast** - no space after cast (`(Type)variable`)
- **In method parameters** - no spaces inside parameter parentheses (`Method(param1, param2)`)

Example:
```csharp
// ✅ Correct
if (condition && otherCondition)
{
    var result = (string)value;
    DoSomething(param1, param2);
}

// ❌ Incorrect
if(condition&&otherCondition)
{
    var result = ( string )value;
    DoSomething( param1, param2 );
}
```

## Comments

- **In English** - all comments should be in English
- **XML comments** - use XML comments for public methods and properties
- **Explain "why"** - comments should explain "why", not "what"

Example:
```csharp
/// <summary>
/// Converts PascalCase/TitleCase to camelCase.
/// Handles leading acronyms intelligently.
/// </summary>
public static string ToCamelCase(this string s)
{
    // Localized default values
    var notSpecified = language switch
    {
        "en" => "Not specified",
        "ru" => "Not specified",
        _ => "Not specified"
    };
}
```

## File structure

- **Namespace at top** - namespace at the beginning of the file
- **File-scoped namespaces** - use file-scoped namespaces if supported (C# 10+)
- **Using order** - System.* directives first, then others

Example:
```csharp
namespace Web.Api.Modules.Vacancies.Controllers;

using System;
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc;

[ApiController]
public class VacanciesController : ControllerBase
{
}
```

## Async/Await

- **Async suffix** - all async methods must have `Async` suffix
- **Use CancellationToken** - pass `CancellationToken` to async methods
- **ConfigureAwait** - do not use `ConfigureAwait(false)` in ASP.NET Core (not required)

Example:
```csharp
public async Task<ApiEnvelope<bool>> SubmitResumeAsync(
    [FromForm] SubmitResumeDto request,
    CancellationToken cancellationToken)
{
    var htmlBody = await File.ReadAllTextAsync(htmlTemplatePath, cancellationToken);
    await _emailSenderService.SendAsync(recipientName, recipientEmail, subject, textBody, htmlBody, cancellationToken);
}
```

## Logging

- **Structured logging** - use parameterized messages
- **Log levels** - use correct levels (`LogInformation`, `LogWarning`, `LogError`)

Example:
```csharp
_logger.LogInformation("Received SubmitResume request. ModelState.IsValid: {IsValid}", ModelState.IsValid);
_logger.LogWarning("ModelState error for {Key}: {Errors}", error.Key, string.Join(", ", errors));
_logger.LogError(ex, "Failed to send email notification");
```

## Exceptions

- **Use specific exception types** - use specific exception types instead of `Exception`
- **Messages in English** - exception messages should be in English (for technical details)

Example:
```csharp
if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(htmlBody))
    throw new Exception("Email templates are not found");

if (!permissionsAuthorized)
    throw new ForbiddenException("Access denied");
```
